    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I want to know what\u2019s the best way to get ready for a run. What should I do before starting?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I prepare to run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To get ready for a run, you should follow these steps:\n\n1. **Hydrate**: Drink some water before your run, especially if it\u2019s in the morning, to combat dehydration from sleeping.\n\n2. **Plan Your Gear**: Lay out your running clothes and shoes the night before to streamline your morning routine.\n\n3. **Warm-Up**: Spend 5-15 minutes on a dynamic warm-up. This can include light jogging, dynamic stretches (like leg swings and arm circles), and aerobic exercises (such as jumping jacks). This helps increase blood flow to your muscles and prepares your body for running.\n\n4. **Nutrition**: For longer runs, have a light snack like a banana or a small breakfast (like oatmeal or toast) at least 30 minutes before you start to avoid gastrointestinal issues.\n\n5. **Cool Down**: After your run, gradually reduce your pace to cool down, followed by walking for 5-10 minutes and stretching.\n\nBy incorporating these practices, you can enhance your running performance and reduce the risk of injury.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0006-62-05770:1": 2.886227607727051,
