      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that helps! What does a typical week of workout look like when preparing for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik": "What does a typical week of workout look like when preparing for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "A typical week of workouts when preparing for a 10 km run can vary, but here's a general outline based on a beginner training plan:\n\n**Monday**: Rest or light cross-training (like cycling or swimming)  \n**Tuesday**: 2.5-mile easy run followed by optional strength training (15-30 minutes)  \n**Wednesday**: 30 minutes of cross-training  \n**Thursday**: 2-mile easy run followed by optional strength training (15-30 minutes)  \n**Friday**: Rest  \n**Saturday**: 40 minutes of cross-training  \n**Sunday**: Long run (starting at 3 miles and gradually increasing each week)\n\nAs you progress, you can incorporate speedwork, such as intervals or tempo runs, to enhance your performance. Make sure to include warm-ups before and cool-downs after each workout to prepare your body and aid recovery.",
          "citations": {
