      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting! Can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When choosing running shoes, it\u2019s essential to prioritize comfort and fit. Here are some key points to consider:\n\n1. **Get Fitted**: Visit a specialty running store where staff can analyze your gait and recommend shoes based on your foot type and running style. This is crucial for injury prevention and comfort.\n\n2. **Consider Your Needs**: Determine if you need shoes for road running, trail running, or a specific type of terrain. Each type of shoe is designed to provide the best support and traction for different surfaces.\n\n3. **Quality Matters**: Invest in a good pair of running shoes. They should have adequate cushioning, support, and a fit that feels snug but not tight. Look for performance materials that wick away moisture to prevent blisters.\n\n4. **Try Before You Buy**: Always try on shoes and walk or jog around the store to see how they feel. Make sure there\u2019s enough room in the toe box and that they don\u2019t pinch your feet.\n\n5. **Replace Regularly**: Running shoes typically need to be replaced every 300-500 miles, depending on your running style and the shoe\u2019s construction. Pay attention to wear patterns to know",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0032-17-06111:8": -0.27640119194984436
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
