            "My granpa worked as a shoemaker"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s useful. What about adjusting my workout if I\u2019m just training for a 5km, not 10km?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When training for a 5K, your workout schedule should focus more on speed and shorter intervals compared to a 10K. Here\u2019s a suggested weekly structure tailored for 5K training:\n\n**Monday**: Rest or light cross-training (like cycling or swimming)  \n**Tuesday**: Speed workout (e.g., 5 x 400 meters at goal 5K pace with 100m jogging rest)  \n**Wednesday**: Easy run (30 minutes at a comfortable pace)  \n**Thursday**: Tempo run (e.g., 2 miles at a pace slightly faster than your goal 5K pace)  \n**Friday**: Rest  \n**Saturday**: Long run (start at 3-4 miles and gradually increase)  \n**Sunday**: Easy recovery run (30 minutes)  \n\nIncorporate interval training, such as 800-meter repeats at your 5K goal pace, with shorter recovery periods, to build your speed endurance. Adjust the intensity based on how you feel, and remember to include warm-ups and cool-downs to prevent injury.",
