        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes sense! What does a typical week of workout look like when preparing for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik": "What does a typical week of workout look like when preparing for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "A typical week of workouts when preparing for a 10 km run can look like this:\n\n**Week 1 Example:**\n- **Monday**: Rest day\n- **Tuesday**: 2.5 miles easy run (followed by optional strength training)\n- **Wednesday**: 30 minutes of cross training (like cycling or swimming)\n- **Thursday**: 2 miles easy run (followed by optional strength training)\n- **Friday**: Rest day\n- **Saturday**: 40 minutes of cross training\n- **Sunday**: 3 miles long run\n\nThis plan gradually increases your mileage and incorporates various types of workouts, including easy runs, cross training, and long runs to build endurance. As you progress, you can add more distance and intensity, such as speedwork or hill training, depending on your comfort level. Make sure to listen to your body and adjust the plan as needed!",
