          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful, thanks. Can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When selecting running shoes, consider the following factors to ensure you find the right pair for your needs:\n\n1. **Fit**: It's crucial to have a proper fit. Generally, you should go at least half a size up from your regular shoe size to allow for toe movement. Ensure there's at least half a thumb's width between your big toe and the end of the shoe.\n\n2. **Arch Support**: Depending on your foot type (flat, normal, or high arches), you may need different levels of arch support. If you have high arches, look for shoes with mild support under the arch to enhance comfort.\n\n3. **Cushioning**: Choose shoes with appropriate cushioning based on your running style. If you are a heel striker, opt for shoes with more cushioning to absorb impact. For forefoot or midfoot strikers, you might prefer shoes with less cushioning as your foot naturally absorbs more shock.\n\n4. **Terrain**: Consider where you\u2019ll be running. Trail running shoes have features like rugged outsoles for grip and protection against debris, while road running shoes are designed for smooth surfaces.\n\n5. **Insoles**: You can also enhance",
