          "user_utterance": "Any recommendations that aren\u2019t Nike? I\u2019ve had some bad luck with them lately.",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "If you're looking for running shoe recommendations outside of Nike, here are some excellent brands to consider:\n\n1. **ASICS**: Known for their quality and support, ASICS shoes are popular among long-distance runners. Models like the GEL-Nimbus and GEL-Kayano offer great cushioning and stability.\n\n2. **Brooks**: This brand focuses solely on running shoes and is well-regarded for comfort and support. The Brooks Ghost and Brooks Adrenaline are favorites among many runners.\n\n3. **Saucony**: With a long history in running footwear, Saucony produces shoes that cater to various running styles. The Saucony Triumph and Saucony Kinvara are highly recommended.\n\n4. **HOKA**: Known for their maximalist cushioning, HOKA shoes provide excellent shock absorption, making them a great choice for those who need extra comfort during their runs.\n\n5. **Mizuno**: Their Wave technology offers a unique balance of cushioning and responsiveness. The Mizuno Wave Rider is a popular model among runners.\n\n6. **On**: This brand features a distinctive design and offers shoes with great cushioning and support. The On Cloudstratus and Cloudflow are",
