      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! I\u2019ll look into Brooks and Asics. How should I adjust my workout for a 5km run instead of 10km?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To adjust your workout for a 5km run instead of a 10km, you should focus more on speed and speed endurance. Here\u2019s a sample week of workouts tailored for a 5km:\n\n**Sample Week for 5km Training:**\n- **Monday**: Rest or light cross-training (like cycling or swimming)\n- **Tuesday**: Speed workout, such as 6 x 400 meters at goal 5km pace with 100m jogging rest between each\n- **Wednesday**: Easy run for 3-4 miles at a comfortable pace\n- **Thursday**: Tempo run, like 20 minutes at a pace slightly faster than your goal 5km pace\n- **Friday**: Rest or strength training\n- **Saturday**: Long run of 4-5 miles at an easy pace\n- **Sunday**: Speed workout, such as 5 x 1000 meters at goal 5km pace with 2-3 minutes rest in between\n\nThis structure emphasizes shorter, faster workouts to build speed while still incorporating some endurance training. Make sure to listen to your body and adjust the intensity and volume as needed!",
          "citations": {
