      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I want to know how to get ready for a run. Any tips?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I prepare to run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To get ready for a run, follow these tips:\n\n1. **Plan Ahead**: The night before, lay out your running clothes and gear. This will save time and help you avoid second-guessing your decision to run.\n\n2. **Hydrate**: Drink extra water after dinner to combat morning dehydration. Aim for about 16 ounces.\n\n3. **Set a Morning Routine**: Allow enough time in the morning to eat a light snack, warm up, and prepare for your run without rushing.\n\n4. **Warm Up**: Spend 5-15 minutes warming up with dynamic stretches like leg swings or lunges, and consider a short walk or light jog to get your muscles ready.\n\n5. **Listen to Music or a Podcast**: Bring some motivation by listening to your favorite tunes or an inspiring podcast while you run.\n\n6. **Cool Down**: After your run, take time to cool down with a slow jog or walk, followed by stretching to help your muscles recover.\n\nBy following these steps, you can make your running experience more enjoyable and effective!",
          "citations": {
