          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Definitely skipping Nike, they never work for me. Do you know any specific Brooks or New Balance models that are good for beginners?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Skipping Nike is a great choice for you, given your past dissatisfaction. For beginner-friendly models, I recommend the Brooks Ghost 14 and the New Balance Fresh Foam 860v12. The Brooks Ghost 14 is known for its comfortable, cushioned fit and versatility, making it ideal for easy runs or longer distances. The New Balance Fresh Foam 860v12 offers excellent support for overpronators and a smooth ride, which is great for beginners seeking stability. Both models are highly rated for everyday training and should suit your 10K preparation well. You can find these at specialty running stores or online retailers.",
