          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To get ready for a run, especially if you're not very confident in your fitness level, start with a gentle warm-up\u201410 to 15 minutes of walking or light jogging is ideal to prepare your muscles and joints [clueweb22-en0021-73-11929:5][clueweb22-en0006-62-05770:9]. Follow this with dynamic stretches such as lunges, butt-kickers, leg lifts, or specific routines for your calves and Achilles, which help increase your range of motion and reduce the risk of injury [clueweb22-en0021-73-11929:5][clueweb22-en0003-11-05343:0]. Avoid static stretching before your run; save those for after. This simple routine will help you feel more comfortable and confident as you start running. Would you like a step-by-step beginner warm-up routine?",
