      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful\u2014thanks. Actually, are there mistakes people often make when picking out running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Many beginners make the mistake of picking running shoes based solely on their usual shoe size, but it's important to size up at least half a size to prevent issues like losing toenails, as feet swell during running [clueweb22-en0012-29-00139:4]. Comfort and fit are crucial\u2014there should be a thumb's width of space between your toes and the end of the shoe, and the shoe should support your foot's natural movement and pronation [clueweb22-en0004-94-13132:12]. Avoid buying shoes just for their looks or from large chain stores; instead, visit a specialty retailer where experts can assess your foot shape and running style for the best match [clueweb22-en0014-95-05002:1]. Lastly, wearing the wrong shoes can lead to joint pain and muscle aches, so always prioritize quality and listen to your body's feedback [clueweb22-en0027-31-13974:13]. Do you want tips for breaking in new running shoes?",
          "citations": {
