  {
    "runtag": "grilllab-agentic-gpt4.1-larf",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "4-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I want to know how I should prepare before going for a run. Any tips?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I prepare to run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To prepare for a run, especially if you're not very confident in your fitness, start with a gentle warm-up to prime your muscles and help prevent injury\u2014this won't make you too tired, but will actually improve your performance [clueweb22-en0010-44-01052:0]. Eat a light snack like half a banana or a small granola bar if you haven't eaten recently, as this can help maintain your energy levels, especially for morning runs [clueweb22-en0008-29-00346:6]. Choose a realistic training plan that fits your current fitness and lifestyle, and don't be afraid to use run-walk intervals as you build confidence and endurance [clueweb22-en0015-87-11093:0][clueweb22-en0015-87-11093:1]. Preparing your gear and planning your post-run routine in advance can also make the process smoother and less stressful. Are you interested in beginner running plans or apps?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0008-29-00346:6": 0.03252247488101534,
            "clueweb22-en0010-44-01052:0": 0.028665028665028666,
            "clueweb22-en0015-87-11093:0": 0.026132699813337858,
            "clueweb22-en0015-87-11093:1": 0.025158227848101268
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I am not very confident in my fitness level.",
            "I am 22 years old."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that's helpful! What does a typical week of workout look like when preparing for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik": "What does a typical week of workout look like when preparing for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For beginners, a standard 10k training week often involves running 3-4 times per week, with at least two rest days to allow for recovery. For example, a 12-week plan might have you run on Tuesday, Thursday, and Sunday, with the Sunday run gradually increasing in distance each week, and rest days on Monday and Saturday [clueweb22-en0021-42-04337:0]. Another approach suggests running at least three times a week, plus one or two days of cross-training (like cycling or swimming) to build fitness and reduce injury risk [clueweb22-en0005-57-00569:2]. It's perfectly fine to use run-walk intervals, especially if you're not confident in your fitness. The key is to increase your long run distance slowly and listen to your body. Intermediate plans may add a speedwork day, but for beginners, focusing on consistency and gradual progress is most important [clueweb22-en0014-61-01516:2]. Do you want advice on running gear for beginners?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0021-42-04337:0": 0.05727114477114477,
            "clueweb22-en0005-57-00569:2": 0.05319918931976422,
            "clueweb22-en0014-61-01516:2": 0.05032847848381829,
            "clueweb22-en0044-68-07928:0": 0.0482965899329659
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I am not very confident in my fitness level."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Yes, can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When selecting running shoes as a beginner, prioritize comfort and fit\u2014your toes shouldn't feel squished, and the shoes should feel supportive but not tight. Popular beginner-friendly models include the Saucony Ride, Brooks Ghost, HOKA Clifton, and ASICS GEL-Cumulus, among others [clueweb22-en0040-46-18574:0]. It's best to visit a running specialist or store where they can assess your foot type, arch height, and gait to recommend the right shoe for you [clueweb22-en0023-70-13273:4]. Avoid using shoes designed for other activities, like HIIT or gym shoes, as they may lack the necessary cushioning and durability for running [clueweb22-en0038-52-20255:10]. Plan to replace your running shoes every 250 miles or when they show significant wear, and break in new shoes gradually with shorter runs [clueweb22-en0023-70-13273:4]. Would you like tips on running socks or other gear?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0040-46-18574:0": 0.025451688923802042,
            "clueweb22-en0038-52-20255:10": 0.023809523809523808,
            "clueweb22-en0032-86-15272:0": 0.022005772005772008,
            "clueweb22-en0023-70-13273:4": 0.021595262974573322
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I am not very confident in my fitness level."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What about socks? Are they important for 5km runs?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "Wearing the right socks is crucial even for shorter runs like 5km. Technical running socks made from polyester-cotton blends or other moisture-wicking materials help reduce moisture and friction, which are the main causes of blisters and discomfort during runs [clueweb22-en0007-65-15080:6]. High-performance socks often have extra cushioning in areas prone to calluses and blisters, enhancing comfort and injury prevention [clueweb22-en0012-54-01556:1]. Compression socks can also provide muscle support and further reduce the risk of blisters and chafing, making them a good option for runners who want extra support and comfort [clueweb22-en0027-08-00711:5]. Avoid regular cotton socks, as they tend to retain moisture and increase the risk of blisters. Do you want advice on other running gear for beginners?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0007-65-15080:6": 0.032018442622950824,
            "clueweb22-en0012-54-01556:1": 0.03131881575727918,
            "clueweb22-en0027-08-00711:5": 0.028782894736842105
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I am not very confident in my fitness level.",
            "I am a beginner runner."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Maybe later. How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run if I get tired easily?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To adjust your 5km workout plan when you get tired easily, try a run-walk program: alternate running and walking (for example, run 2 minutes, walk 2 minutes) and repeat until you complete your session. This method helps your body adapt gradually and reduces fatigue [clueweb22-en0029-39-07581:9][clueweb22-en0012-57-12883:6]. Choose a beginner-friendly plan that builds up mileage and intensity slowly, and don't hesitate to take extra rest days or cross-train with activities like cycling or swimming to improve your overall fitness without overexertion [clueweb22-en0012-57-12883:6][clueweb22-en0019-16-15604:0]. Remember, it's okay to modify any plan to fit your needs\u2014consistency and listening to your body are key. Do you want advice on nutrition or hydration for running?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0009-99-13195:4": 0.03200204813108039,
            "clueweb22-en0012-57-12883:6": 0.02946236559139785,
            "clueweb22-en0019-16-15604:0": 0.027777777777777776,
            "clueweb22-en0029-39-07581:9": 0.027623285131627734
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I am not very confident in my fitness level."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thank you for all the helpful information! I have all I need for now. Wishing you the best with your running\u2014stay healthy and enjoy your workouts. Farewell!",
          "user_rubrik": null,
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
