      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I'm looking for tips on how to prepare for a run. Any suggestions?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I prepare to run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To prepare for a run\u2014especially if you\u2019re not confident in your fitness\u2014focus on these essentials:\n\n**1. Warm Up Thoroughly**\n- Start with 5\u201310 minutes of brisk walking or light jogging to get your body ready (crucial for injury prevention and performance).\n- Add dynamic stretches (like lunges, leg swings, or butt-kickers) to activate major muscle groups and increase range of motion.\n\n**2. Hydration & Nutrition**\n- Drink water before your run, even if you don\u2019t feel thirsty (important in both hot and cold weather).\n- Eat a light, carb-rich meal 2\u20134 hours before running; avoid heavy or high-fiber foods if you\u2019re prone to stomach issues.\n\n**3. Dress for Comfort**\n- Wear moisture-wicking clothes to help manage sweat and reduce irritation, which can also help with summer runny nose by keeping you cool and dry.\n\n**4. Address Runny Nose**\n- Consider using a sweatband or carrying tissues.\n- Running in the early morning or after rain can reduce pollen exposure, which may help",
