      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks for the tips! What kind of nutrition should I focus on before and after a run?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "For your first runs, focus on simple, allergy-safe nutrition that supports energy, recovery, and your comfort:\n\n**Before Your Run**\n- **Timing:** Eat a light, carb-focused snack 30\u201360 minutes before running (e.g., banana, toast with jam, low-fiber cereal). Avoid high-fiber or high-fat foods to reduce stomach upset ([clueweb22-en0039-23-01537], [clueweb22-en0031-24-03437]).\n- **Carbs:** Prioritize easily digestible carbohydrates for quick energy (fruit, white bread, rice cakes).\n- **Hydration:** Drink water before you head out ([clueweb22-en0030-59-14446]).\n\n**After Your Run**\n- **Carbs + Protein:** Within 30\u201345 minutes, have a snack or meal with both carbs and protein to speed recovery and muscle repair ([clueweb22-en0001-29-15914], [clueweb22-en0040-39-17535]).\n    - Safe options: yogurt with fruit",
