      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Sounds good! Any specific stretches I should incorporate after my run?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "For post-run stretching\u2014especially as a beginner with fitness concerns\u2014focus on simple, static stretches targeting the main running muscles. This helps reduce soreness, improve flexibility, and aids recovery (clueweb22-en0033-65-07075, clueweb22-en0036-22-19114).\n\n**Key Stretches to Include After Your Run:**\n- **Quads:** Stand, pull one foot toward your glutes, keeping knees together.\n- **Hamstrings:** Sit or stand, reach gently toward your toes with a straight back.\n- **Calves:** Lean into a wall with one leg extended behind, heel flat.\n- **Hip Flexors:** Kneel on one knee, gently push hips forward.\n- **Glutes:** Lying on your back, cross one ankle over the opposite knee and pull the thigh toward you.\n\n**How to Stretch:**\n- Hold each stretch for 30\u201360 seconds.\n- Stretch only to mild tension, not pain.\n- Breathe deeply and relax into each position.\n\n**Why This Matters for You:**\n- These stretches",
