          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Nice! What should I consider when choosing running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When choosing running shoes\u2014especially as a beginner not confident in your fitness\u2014prioritize comfort, fit, and support. Here\u2019s what matters most for you:\n\n**1. Comfort & Fit**\n- Shoes should feel immediately comfortable; avoid anything tight, loose, or that causes pressure points ([Fleet Feet], [Jogging Addiction]).\n- Try on several brands and models\u2014everyone\u2019s feet are different. Don\u2019t assume what works for others will work for you ([Fleet Feet], [Tagalong]).\n\n**2. Support & Cushioning**\n- Look for shoes with good cushioning to reduce impact and lower injury risk, especially if you\u2019re easing into running ([New Balance Fresh Foam], [Brooks Ghost 14], [HOKA Clifton 8]).\n- If you have flat feet or need extra support, consider models with built-in arch support or that accommodate orthotics ([Brooks Glycerin GTS 20], [New Balance 1080]).\n\n**3. Gait & Specialty Fitting**\n- If possible, visit a specialty running store for a gait analysis. This ensures the",
