          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great points! What are some common mistakes to avoid when preparing for my first run?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Here\u2019s what to watch out for when preparing for your first run, especially given your fitness confidence and tendency for a runny nose:\n\n**Top Mistakes to Avoid**\n\n- **Skipping the Warm-Up:** Not warming up is a leading cause of injury. Always start with 5\u201310 minutes of brisk walking or dynamic stretches to prep your muscles and joints ([ProForm], [Fit People]).\n- **Overdoing It:** Doing too much, too soon (long runs, running every day) can lead to burnout or injury. Stick to gradual increases and allow rest days ([SELF], [ProForm]).\n- **Ignoring Your Body:** Pushing through pain or discomfort can cause setbacks. Listen to your body and rest if you feel pain or excessive fatigue ([ProForm], [Fit People]).\n- **Wearing the Wrong Shoes or Clothes:** Ill-fitting shoes or non-breathable clothing can cause blisters, discomfort, or even injury. Choose running-specific shoes and moisture-wicking gear ([Fit People]).\n- **Neglecting Hydration/Nutrition:** Not drinking enough water or eating too close",
