      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Cool, that\u2019s clear. How much should I run per week if I want to do a 10k?",
          "user_rubrik": "What does a typical week of workout look like when preparing for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 4,
          "text": "For a 10K, it's generally recommended to have a total weekly mileage base of about 8 miles, with your longest run at about 3 miles, for at least a month before starting a training program. As you progress, you can aim to run around 15 miles per week, spread over at least three runs. However, this can vary depending on your current fitness level and running experience. It's essential to gradually increase your mileage to avoid fatigue and injury. If you're a complete beginner, consider starting with a \"couch to 10K\" training schedule to help you build up your endurance. Remember to listen to your body and adjust your training plan accordingly.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0043-66-10746:9": 8.179424285888672,
