      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Nice, I\u2019ll check those out, thanks. Shifting a bit\u2014how do I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For a 5km run, you can start with a basic training plan that includes three workouts per week, with at least two days of rest or alternative training in between. Begin with shorter runs and gradually increase the distance and intensity over time. A typical plan may include a mix of running, walking, and rest days, with the goal of building up to a 30-minute continuous run. You can also incorporate interval training, hill repeats, and tempo runs to improve your speed and endurance. Remember to listen to your body and adjust the plan as needed to avoid injury or burnout. A general rule of thumb is to increase your weekly mileage by no more than 10% each week. With consistent training and gradual progression, you can be ready for a 5km run in about 8 weeks.   Please let me know if I can assist you further.",
