      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! That\u2019s more useful. What about warming up before running? What should I do exactly?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I prepare to run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To warm up before running, start with some light cardio such as jogging in place or jumping jacks to get your heart rate up and blood flowing. Then, move on to dynamic stretching exercises like leg swings, arm circles, and hip rotations to loosen up your muscles. You can also do some specific running drills like high knees, butt kicks, and lunges to prepare your muscles for the run. The goal is to get your body moving and warm without exhausting yourself before the actual run. Keep your warm-up routine short and sweet, around 10-15 minutes, and finish it up just before you start your run.",
