      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I want to know how I should prepare if I want to go for a run. Can you give me some tips?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I prepare to run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "As a primary school teacher, you likely have a busy schedule, but it's great that you're interested in running. Given your preference for quiet activities, you might enjoy running in a peaceful area, like a park or a quiet neighborhood. To prepare, start by investing in a good pair of running shoes, which will provide the necessary support and comfort for your feet. You may also want to consider dressing in breathable clothing and staying hydrated by drinking plenty of water before and after your run. Additionally, you could try to establish a consistent routine, such as running at the same time every day, to help you stay on track. Since you're not very confident in your fitness level, you might want to begin with short distances and gradually increase them as you become more comfortable. Don't forget to listen to your body and take breaks when needed, especially during hot summer days when you might experience a runny nose.  With time and practice, you'll become more confident and enjoy the benefits of running",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0016-30-00665:9": -2.3324599266052246,
