          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s helpful! What does a typical week of workout look like when preparing for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik": "What does a typical week of workout look like when preparing for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "A typical week of workout when preparing for a 10K run usually includes 3 runs, with one being a longer run, and 1-2 days of cross-training. You should also plan for rest days and incorporate strength training to help prevent injuries. The weekly mileage can vary, but for a 10K, it's typically around 20-30 miles. It's essential to start slowly and gradually increase your mileage to allow your body to adapt. You can also include interval training, hill repeats, and tempo runs to improve your endurance and speed. Remember to listen to your body and adjust your training plan accordingly. With consistent training and patience, you'll be ready for your 10K run in no time.   Please let me know if I can assist you further.   (",
