          "user_utterance": "Yeah, my grandpa used to talk a lot about how important a good fit and solid construction are. I\u2019ve noticed that Nike shoes usually let me down though. Is there a brand or type you think works best for beginner runners like me?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "As a beginner runner, you may want to consider brands like Asics or Saucony, which are known for their supportive and comfortable shoes. The Asics Gel series or the Saucony Cohesion line could be a good starting point. These shoes often provide a balance of cushioning and stability, making them suitable for runners who are just starting out. Since you've had disappointing experiences with Nike, it might be worth exploring other options to find the right fit for you. Additionally, visiting a specialty running store can help you find the perfect shoe based on your foot type and running style.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0019-82-06673:11": 1.7074520587921143,
            "clueweb22-en0009-82-15496:6": 1.2073358297348022,
            "clueweb22-en0001-37-09896:14": 0.4135330021381378,
            "clueweb22-en0031-15-00155:1": 0.3216223120689392,
            "clueweb22-en0010-29-14731:12": 0.23013871908187866
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! I often get a runny nose when I run outside, especially in summer. Is there a way to prevent or handle that?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "You can try wearing a face mask or applying a nasal spray before running to help reduce the symptoms of a runny nose. Additionally, running in the early morning or evening when the air is cooler and less humid may also help alleviate the issue. If your runny nose is caused by allergies, you may want to consider taking an antihistamine medication before your run. It's also essential to stay hydrated by drinking plenty of water to thin out the mucus and make it easier to expel. By taking these precautions, you can help minimize the discomfort of a runny nose and enjoy your runs more.   Please let me know if I can assist you further.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0011-78-03972:3": 5.283445358276367,
            "clueweb22-en0016-68-14805:1": 4.345579147338867,
            "clueweb22-en0046-30-14030:8": 4.252407550811768,
            "clueweb22-en0016-68-14805:2": 3.8653719425201416,
            "clueweb22-en0040-47-06246:0": 3.696559190750122
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Nice tips! Could you explain more about adjusting my workout plan for a 5km run? I want to know exactly how to make a plan for that distance.",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To create a workout plan for a 5km run, start by determining your current fitness level and running experience. A typical plan includes 3-4 runs per week, with one longer run, and incorporates rest days and cross-training. You can begin with shorter distances and gradually increase them as you become more comfortable. It's essential to include a mix of easy runs, speed workouts, and strength training to improve your endurance and speed. Consider your schedule and lifestyle, and adjust the plan accordingly. For example, you can schedule your long run on a Sunday, followed by a rest day, and then start your short, base runs on Monday. Remember to listen to your body and make adjustments as needed to avoid injury and ensure a successful 5km run.   Please let me know if I can assist you further.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0036-88-06294:3": 3.7000603675842285,
            "clueweb22-en0026-22-13925:10": 3.6766271591186523,
            "clueweb22-en0032-98-08326:14": 3.4552242755889893,
            "clueweb22-en0004-95-09067:14": 3.321190118789673,
            "clueweb22-en0004-46-17802:3": 2.710510730743408
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
