  {
    "runtag": "orga-llama70b-bm25-minilm-llama70b",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "4-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I'm trying to figure out how to get ready for a run. Where should I start?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I prepare to run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "To increase your running stamina and speed within 2-3 months, start by training on alternate days and gradually increase your running distance and intensity. You can begin with short runs and incorporate walk breaks in between. As you progress, focus on running longer distances without stopping. It's also essential to listen to your body and rest when needed.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0029-77-01786:4": -3.0641305446624756,
            "clueweb22-en0008-32-00126:15": -3.654292345046997,
            "clueweb22-en0023-65-00169:10": -3.6680970191955566,
            "clueweb22-en0041-05-12592:12": -5.8055877685546875,
            "clueweb22-en0004-97-09176:0": -5.857545375823975
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s a bit general. Can you tell me what to do right before a run? Like, any routines or things to avoid?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I prepare to run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Right before a run, it's a good idea to have a light snack to boost your energy levels. You can try something like a half-banana with nut butter or a small granola bar, but be sure to avoid peanuts due to your allergy. Also, make sure to get your gear ready, including your clothes and any other essentials you need for your run. Having a routine can help you feel more prepared and get into the right mindset for your run. Additionally, consider doing some dynamic stretches or range of motion exercises to help prevent injuries and get your body ready for the run.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0044-67-01636:7": 2.1171517372131348,
            "clueweb22-en0044-45-02109:1": 2.0716772079467773,
            "clueweb22-en0023-36-03858:9": 1.5967687368392944,
            "clueweb22-en0008-29-00346:6": 1.3990483283996582,
            "clueweb22-en0011-22-15479:15": 0.6686545610427856
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks. About a whole week of prepping for a 10 km run\u2014what should my workout schedule look like?",
          "user_rubrik": "What does a typical week of workout look like when preparing for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For a 10km run, your weekly schedule can include a mix of rest days, easy runs, and paced workouts. You can start with 2-3 runs per week, with one longer run on the weekends, and incorporate cross-training or rest days in between. For example, you can have easy runs on Tuesdays and Thursdays, a longer run on Sundays, and rest or cross-train on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Fridays. Make sure to also include warm-ups, cool-downs, and stretching exercises to help prevent injuries and improve your overall performance. As you get closer to the 10km run, you can adjust your schedule to include more paced workouts and longer runs to build up your endurance. It's also essential to listen to your body and rest when needed to avoid burnout and injury.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0016-60-18715:1": 2.6057748794555664,
            "clueweb22-en0013-68-19634:0": 2.4655041694641113,
            "clueweb22-en0020-49-07951:9": 2.3409252166748047,
            "clueweb22-en0006-99-01338:3": 2.2812423706054688,
            "clueweb22-en0023-65-04695:11": 2.2264435291290283
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "As a runner, it's essential to find the right shoe that fits your foot type and running style. You may want to consider visiting a specialty running store where they can help you determine your foot type and gait, and recommend the best shoe for you. Some popular brands include Adidas, Asics, and New Balance, which offer a range of models with different features such as cushioning, support, and stability. Since you mentioned you're not very confident in your fitness level, you may want to start with a shoe that provides extra support and stability. Additionally, given your grandpa's background as a shoemaker, you may have a keen eye for quality and craftsmanship in a shoe. It's also worth noting that different brands have different sizing, so it's crucial to try on several options to find the best fit.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0004-80-02749:7": 3.5448968410491943,
            "clueweb22-en0037-87-04180:9": 3.2105202674865723,
            "clueweb22-en0026-25-17128:4": 2.660942792892456,
            "clueweb22-en0026-48-16143:10": 2.441041946411133,
            "clueweb22-en0029-84-17404:1": 2.4248833656311035
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I usually end up disappointed when I try Nike\u2014do you have any tips for picking good running shoes that last? Maybe other brands or what to check in the store?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Considering your disappointment with Nike, you may want to explore other brands like Adidas, Asics, or New Balance. When trying on shoes, ensure a comfortable fit with enough room for your toes. Check the cushioning, support, and stability features that suit your running style. Also, look for durable materials and a sturdy sole. It's essential to try on several options and go for a run or walk around the store to ensure the shoes feel right. Given your grandpa's shoemaking background, you might appreciate the craftsmanship and quality of certain brands. Don't hesitate to ask for recommendations from a specialty running store staff, as they can help you find the perfect fit.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0031-22-13114:1": 1.427038311958313,
            "clueweb22-en0044-62-09181:1": 1.1361435651779175,
            "clueweb22-en0045-59-03521:1": 0.808249294757843,
            "clueweb22-en0027-80-18835:6": 0.6905028820037842,
            "clueweb22-en0045-08-00015:11": 0.48759472370147705
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Got it, thanks. What kind of stretches should I do before running? I\u2019d like to avoid injuries.",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "Before running, it's a good idea to do some dynamic stretches to help prevent injuries and get your body ready. You can try leg swings, hip circles, and calf raises. These types of stretches can help loosen up your muscles and improve your range of motion. Additionally, you can also do some light stretching to focus on your calf, hamstrings, groin, and quadriceps. Remember to start slowly and gently, and don't bounce or force your muscles beyond a comfortable point. It's also essential to listen to your body and stop if you experience any pain or discomfort. By incorporating these stretches into your pre-run routine, you can help reduce your risk of injury and improve your overall performance.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0031-25-13157:5": 6.147266387939453,
            "clueweb22-en0004-50-04713:2": 6.147032737731934,
            "clueweb22-en0021-49-07779:17": 5.3889617919921875,
            "clueweb22-en0008-07-05825:11": 5.360251426696777,
            "clueweb22-en0045-45-10957:11": 5.339727401733398
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Good pointers. One thing\u2014I always get a runny nose when I run in summer. Is there any way to deal with that?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "To deal with a runny nose while running in summer, you can try using a saline nasal spray to moisten your nasal passages before your run. This can help prevent excess mucus production. You can also try applying a vapor rub or using a humidifier to add moisture to the air, which can help alleviate congestion. Additionally, drinking plenty of fluids to thin out your mucus and using a warm, moist cloth to loosen up any blockages may also help. If your runny nose persists, you may want to consider speaking with a healthcare professional to rule out any underlying allergies or conditions.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0012-56-14869:6": 3.1410083770751953,
            "clueweb22-en0019-59-09825:7": 2.731502056121826,
            "clueweb22-en0023-71-13871:2": 2.469233989715576,
            "clueweb22-en0040-16-11294:6": 1.8374528884887695,
            "clueweb22-en0006-35-02215:0": 1.7312021255493164
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thank you for all your helpful suggestions and questions! You\u2019ve provided great insights on shoes, stretching, and training. If you need more advice in the future, feel free to reach out. Best of luck with your running\u2014take care and happy running!",
          "user_rubrik": null,
