    "runtag": "orga-llama8b-bm25-minilm-llama8b-v2",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "4-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I want to prepare for a run, but I\u2019m not sure where to start. What are the basics?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I prepare to run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To prepare for a run, you should start by building up your endurance. Begin with short walks and gradually increase the duration and intensity over time. It's also essential to incorporate stretching and strengthening exercises to improve your flexibility and overall fitness. Consider consulting with a fitness professional or a running coach to create a personalized training plan tailored to your needs and goals. Additionally, make sure to invest in proper running gear, including comfortable shoes and breathable clothing. Lastly, don't forget to stay hydrated and fuel your body with a balanced diet. Remember, consistency and patience are key when it comes to building a running habit. Start with small achievable goals, and you'll be on your way to becoming a confident runner in no time. Good luck!  Document ID: Doc1, Doc2, Doc3, Doc4, Doc5",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0036-83-00803:16": -1.8714251518249512,
            "clueweb22-en0033-34-10821:1": -3.53191876411438,
            "clueweb22-en0008-78-12995:11": -3.6810126304626465,
            "clueweb22-en0022-02-19889:2": -3.8109261989593506,
            "clueweb22-en0033-34-10821:0": -3.984592914581299
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that helps! What does a typical week of workout look like when preparing for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik": "What does a typical week of workout look like when preparing for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "A typical week of workout when preparing for a 10 km run should include a mix of aerobic and strength training routines. Warm up before each workout with \u2153 to \u00bd of the total distance, and include active recovery periods between intervals. For example, you can start with a 5-minute jog or brisk walk, followed by 1 mile at 90% of your maximum pace, and then actively recover with 7-10 minutes of jogging or walking. Repeat this pattern and cool down with stretching, jogging, or brisk walking for 5 minutes. As you progress, you can increase the intensity and duration of your workouts. It's also essential to listen to your body and not push yourself too hard, especially if you're new to running. Start with shorter distances and gradually build up to longer runs. Remember to include rest days and cross-training to avoid burnout and prevent injuries. Consistency and patience are key when it comes to building up to a 10 km run. Choose",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0023-65-04695:11": 2.7663140296936035,
            "clueweb22-en0020-17-10574:2": 1.7683169841766357,
