          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes sense. Can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When preparing for a run, it's essential to invest in proper running shoes. You should choose shoes that provide comfort, support, and stability. As a beginner, you may not need the most advanced technology, but a good pair of shoes can make a significant difference in your running experience. Consider visiting a specialty running store where knowledgeable staff can help you find the right fit and provide guidance on the best shoes for your foot type and running style. Additionally, make sure to break in your new shoes before wearing them for a long run. A good rule of thumb is to log at least 60 to 80 miles on your shoes before racing in them. This will help prevent blisters and discomfort during your run. Don't forget to also consider the terrain you'll be running on and choose shoes that are suitable for the conditions. With the right shoes, you'll be able to focus on your training and enjoy the experience of running. Choose shoes that feel comfortable and supportive, and don't be afraid",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0029-77-01786:4": 0.18346525728702545,
            "clueweb22-en0010-34-08119:8": -0.7736407518386841,
