          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great, I\u2019ll look into those. What adjustments should I make if I\u2019m training for a 5km run instead of a longer distance?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When training for a 5km run, you can focus on shorter and more intense workouts. Aim for 3-4 runs per week, with one longer run on the weekends. For example, you can start with a 5-minute jog or brisk walk, followed by 1-2 minutes of high-intensity running, and then recover with 2-3 minutes of walking or jogging. Repeat this pattern for a total of 20-30 minutes. As you progress, you can increase the intensity and duration of your workouts. It's also essential to include strength training and stretching exercises to improve your overall fitness and prevent injuries. Remember to listen to your body and not push yourself too hard, especially if you're new to running. Start with shorter distances and gradually build up to longer runs. Choose a training plan that suits your needs and goals, and don't forget to stay hydrated and fuel your body with a balanced diet. With consistent training and patience, you'll be ready to crush",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0008-57-08667:3": 0.34250107407569885,
