    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m interested in running, but I don\u2019t really know how to get ready for it. What should I do?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I prepare to run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Starting to run is a great way to improve your fitness step-by-step! Since you\u2019re new to running, begin with a gentle routine. Start by walking briskly for 5 minutes to warm up, then alternate between 1 minute of jogging and 2 minutes of walking. Gradually increase the jogging time as you feel more comfortable. Aim for 20-30 minutes total, 3 times a week.  Make sure you have comfortable running shoes with good support\u2014since you\u2019re often disappointed with Nike, maybe try brands like New Balance or Asics. Stretch lightly before and after your run to avoid injury, and stay hydrated.  Because you prefer fish and have peanut allergies, fueling your body with balanced meals rich in protein and carbs after running will help recovery. Also, since you enjoy naps at lunchtime, a short rest after running can aid muscle repair.  Start slow, listen to your body, and celebrate small progress. You\u2019ll build confidence and endurance over time!",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      }
    ],
    "judgment": {
