  {
    "runtag": "orga-no-no-no-gpt41mini",
    "type": "ikat-fragment-v1",
    "topic": "4-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful, thanks! What does a typical week of workouts look like if I\u2019m getting ready for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik": "What does a typical week of workout look like when preparing for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "A typical week preparing for a 10 km run would gradually build your endurance while allowing time to recover. Here\u2019s a simple plan:  **Day 1:** Easy run\u2014start with 3-4 km at a comfortable pace, focusing on steady breathing.   **Day 2:** Rest or light cross-training like walking or cycling to avoid overuse injuries.   **Day 3:** Interval training\u2014alternate 3 minutes of faster running with 2 minutes of walking or slow jogging, repeat 4-5 times.   **Day 4:** Rest or gentle stretching/yoga to aid recovery.   **Day 5:** Longer run\u2014gradually increase distance each week, starting at 5 km and adding about 1 km weekly.   **Day 6:** Rest or light activity like an easy walk or a nap to recharge.   **Day 7:** Optional fun activity\u2014visit a flea market or a quiet museum to relax your mind.  Remember to warm up and cool down every session, keep hydrated, and listen to your body. Consistency is key, and incorporating rest will help you avoid injury as your fitness improves.",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      }
    ],
    "judgment": {
      "subtopic-justification": "Good it uses km!",
      "engagement": "Functional Tool",
