      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great, thank you! Can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Absolutely! When choosing running shoes, comfort and fit are the most important factors, especially since you're just starting out. Look for shoes that provide good arch support and cushioning to absorb impact, which helps protect your joints. Since you\u2019ve been disappointed with Nike before, consider brands like Asics, New Balance, Brooks, or Saucony\u2014they\u2019re known for quality running shoes with various fit options.  Make sure to try shoes in the afternoon or evening, as feet tend to swell throughout the day. Wear the same type of socks you plan to run in when trying shoes. There should be about a thumb's width of space between your longest toe and the shoe front to prevent discomfort during your runs.  If possible, visit a specialty running store where experts can analyze your gait and recommend shoes suited to your barefoot shape and running style. Also, since you prefer using cash, you might want to check local stores rather than online.  Replace running shoes every 500-800 km to maintain support and reduce injury risk. Starting with the right pair will make running more enjoyable!",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      }
    ],
    "judgment": {
