      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful, thanks. The last answer wasn\u2019t helpful. More specifically: how can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To adjust your workout plan for a 5km run, focus on higher intensity and speed. Your 5km race pace will be faster than your 10km pace, typically about 15 seconds per mile quicker. Incorporate shorter, faster interval training (e.g., 400m-800m repeats) at or above your 5km goal pace with shorter recovery jogs. Also, include tempo runs at a pace slightly slower than your 5km race pace to build speed endurance. You'll emphasize building anaerobic threshold and speed more than pure endurance.",
          "citations": {
