          "user_utterance": "Got it. Can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For training for a 10 km run, look for lightweight, supportive, and flexible running shoes that offer comfort and durability. Shoes typically last 300-500 miles and should be broken in before a race. It's best to try on different pairs at a running store to find the right fit for your foot type (neutral or stability). Some shoes suitable for 10km include the Adidas Solar Boost, Nike Free RN 5.0 2020, Saucony Cohesion 13, and Nike Downshifter 11.",
