      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s quite a few to consider\u2014thanks! How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run, then?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To adjust your 10 km workout plan for a 5 km run, focus on increasing speed and intensity over shorter distances. Your 5 km race pace will be faster, roughly 8-10 seconds per kilometer quicker than your 10 km pace. For speed work, incorporate shorter, faster intervals (e.g., 400m or 800m) at or above your 5 km goal pace, with shorter recovery periods. While still including easy runs and a long run, the emphasis shifts to building speed endurance and improving your anaerobic threshold for the 5 km distance.",
