      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I actually wanted to know how to prepare before going for a run. What do most people usually do?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I prepare to run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Before a run, most people typically warm up with 5-15 minutes of light jogging and dynamic stretches like lunges or leg swings to prevent injury and get muscles ready. It's also common to check your footwear, ensure laces are tied, and make a bathroom stop. For longer runs, consume easily digestible foods like a banana or oatmeal at least 30 minutes prior, and stay well-hydrated. Some runners also incorporate foam rolling to prepare their muscles.",
