        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful, thanks! What does a typical week of workout look like when preparing for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik": "What does a typical week of workout look like when preparing for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "A typical weekly workout plan for a 10 km run usually involves 3-5 running sessions, including easy runs, a longer endurance run, and speed work like intervals or tempo runs. Many plans also incorporate 1-2 strength and conditioning sessions (around 40-45 minutes) to prevent injury. It's crucial to include 1-3 rest days and have active recovery weeks every fourth week to allow your body to adapt. Training should build gradually, increasing mileage by no more than 10% weekly.",
