          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful, thanks! What about routines\u2014how should I split up my week if I\u2019m aiming for a 10k?",
          "user_rubrik": "What does a typical week of workout look like when preparing for a 10 km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For a 10k training routine, a common approach involves 5 days of running per week: two easy runs, one speedwork session, one long run, and one recovery run. You can fit these around two rest or cross-training days. For example, Monday and Thursday could be rest days, with easy runs on Tuesday and Friday, speedwork on Wednesday, a long run on Saturday, and a recovery run on Sunday. Beginners might start with 3-4 running days, incorporating cross-training and strength.",
