      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s clear. Actually, could you help me with adjusting my workout plan if I want to prepare for a shorter 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To adjust your 10k plan for a 5k, reduce your overall weekly mileage and daily run times. For a 5k, aim for 10-25 miles per week with daily runs of 20-40 minutes, compared to 25-30 miles and 40-50 minutes for a 10k. Your \"long run\" will be shorter. While speedwork is still crucial, it may focus more on efforts at your 5k race pace. Many 5k plans are also typically shorter in duration, often 4-10 weeks.",
          "citations": {
