          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting. Any tips for choosing between different brands or features? I\u2019ve had bad luck with Nike before.",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Given your past experience with Nike, it's good to remember that comfort and fit are the most crucial factors, as there's no single 'perfect' running shoe. Many runners find certain brands work better for them than others. It's highly recommended to visit a specialty running shoe store. They can perform a gait analysis to understand your foot mechanics and recommend shoes tailored to your needs, rather than focusing on specific brands. Try on various brands like Brooks, ASICS, Hoka, New Balance, Mizuno, or Saucony. Focus on how the shoe feels, ensuring enough toe room and comfortable cushioning, rather than just looks or brand marketing.",
