      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Brooks Adrenaline sounds like something I'd try. Do people usually need special insoles, or are the factory ones good enough?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some information about running shoes?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "Brooks running shoes, including the Adrenaline GTS, typically feature removable factory insoles that offer cushioning. While these are often sufficient for many runners, special insoles or custom orthotics are commonly used for enhanced arch support, additional cushioning, or to address specific foot issues like flat feet, high arches, plantar fasciitis, or shin splints. The need for special insoles depends on your individual comfort and foot mechanics.",
