      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I love the idea of new routes. But what do you think about running during hot Spanish summers? Any tips for surviving that?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I adjust my workout plan for a 5km run?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Running in hot Spanish summers requires smart planning. Avoid the hottest part of the day; aim for early mornings or late evenings. Hydrate thoroughly before, during, and after your run. Slow down your pace, as the heat will affect your performance. Wear light-colored, lightweight, and breathable clothing, ideally made of sweat-wicking synthetic fabrics. Seek out shaded routes, and consider reflective gear if running in low light. Cooling off with a cold shower post-run can also help.",
