          "text": "good \u2014 here \u2019 s a compact guide to picking running shoes for a beginner : - fit : get a half - to - full size larger than your everyday shoes so toes have room ( test in the afternoon when feet are a bit swollen ). there should be about a thumb \u2019 s width at the toe. - type : choose road shoes for pavement, trail shoes for uneven dirt. neutral shoes suit most beginners ; choose stability shoes if you overpronate ( store gait analysis helps ). - cushioning & drop : more cushioning feels softer for long runs ; heel - to - toe drop ( 4 \u2013 12 mm ) affects stride \u2014 higher drops suit heel strikers, lower drops feel more natural. - support & weight : lighter shoes feel springier ; more support / cushion = more comfort if you \u2019 re not confident in fitness yet. - try before buying : run 10 \u2013 15 minutes in - store or on a treadmill ; buy from a specialty shop for advice. - socks & lacing : breathable socks and good lacing prevent blisters. - lifespan : replace shoes around 500 \u2013 800 km. rotate two pairs if possible. - brands to consider : asics, brooks, saucony, new balance,",
